Synchronous: Code runs line by line, blocking the next line until the current line finishes.
Example:

console.log("Start");
console.log("End");


Output:

Start
End

-------------------------------
Asynchronous: Code can start an operation and move on without waiting for it to finish. The result comes later through callbacks, promises, or async/await.
Example:

console.log("Start");
setTimeout(() => {
  console.log("Inside Timeout");
}, 1000);
console.log("End");


Output:

Start
End
Inside Timeout